# Nothing here is required. With an empty file the app runs on its rules
# and templates, and the browser's own voice reads aloud.
#
# The model is found in this order: mlx → ollama → hosted → none.

# --- The model: our own 4-bit Qwen on Apple silicon (MLX) -------------------
#   npm run llm:quantize   # once: Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct → 4-bit, into .models/
#   npm run llm:serve      # http://localhost:8080
# MLX_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080
# MLX_MODEL=qwen2.5-1.5b-instruct-4bit
# MLX_TIMEOUT_MS=20000
# How long a child may wait for the next puzzle before the rules plan it.
# LEARN_PLAN_BUDGET_MS=9000

# --- Or Ollama on this machine -----------------------------------------------
#   ollama pull llama3.2:3b
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
# OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.2:3b
# OLLAMA_TIMEOUT_MS=20000

# --- Or any hosted OpenAI-compatible endpoint --------------------------------
# All three together; with one missing it reports itself unavailable.
# HOSTED_LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com/v1
# HOSTED_LLM_API_KEY=
# HOSTED_LLM_MODEL=

# --- The voice: one child's voice, Qwen3-TTS on Apple silicon ---------------
#   npm run tts:serve      # http://localhost:8091 (first run downloads ~2.7 GB)
# TTS_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8091

# --- Pin one model provider instead of the order above -----------------------
# LLM_PROVIDER=mlx
